External programs SplatRAG requires at runtime
----------------------------------------------

These are not Rust crates, so `cargo metadata` does not list them. SplatRAG does not bundle,
redistribute or link them — it makes HTTP calls to servers you start yourself — but it does not
function without them, so they are credited here.

  llama.cpp / llama-server    MIT    https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

Used for both local model roles: the embedding server on :8081 and the basin-labeling / vision
server on :8082 (see `start.sh`). Also used for gemma-diffusion testing during this project's
research. The OCR path in `src/embedding.rs` depends on llama.cpp's `--mmproj` multimodal projector
support.

  Qdrant                      Apache-2.0    https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant

Optional. `src/qdrant.rs` talks to it over HTTP for scoped cosine search when
`[qdrant] enabled = true` and something is listening. SplatRAG degrades to local-only when it is
absent.


