nalgebra (BSD-3-Clause)
-----------------------

The only non-MIT/Apache dependency. BSD-3-Clause carries a no-endorsement clause: nalgebra's authors
and contributors have not endorsed SplatRAG, and their names must not be used to promote it. We do
not redistribute nalgebra's source; it is resolved from crates.io at build time.

nalgebra provides the quaternion and vector math behind splat orientation in `src/geometry.rs`.


fast-hnsw (MIT)
---------------

Provides the approximate-nearest-neighbour graph that `src/ann.rs` wraps as `KeyedAnn`. SplatRAG uses
it with UUID strings as labels so that identity is stable across index rebuilds — insertion order is
an internal detail of the crate and is deliberately not relied upon.


tantivy (MIT)
-------------

Provides the BM25 lexical index in `src/lexical.rs`, which is one of the two arms of the hybrid
retrieval this project is built around.


Prior art this project builds on
--------------------------------

The inversion operators in `src/inversion.rs` are ported from measurements made in
https://github.com/Ruffian-L/ontological-inversion rather than re-derived. The 64D packet and
Unicode/VQ transport contract follows the niodv4 line of work. Attribution for the people and
systems involved is in CREDITS.md.
